{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 76,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.76.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.76.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To the chief Musician on Neginoth, A Psalm ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "or",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Song of Asaph. In Judah ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " God known: his name ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " great in Israel.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.76.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.76.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In Salem also is his tabernacle, and his dwelling place in Zion.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.76.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.76.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There he broke the arrows of the bow, the shield, and the sword, and the battle. Selah.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.76.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.76.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "art",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " more glorious ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " excellent than the mountains of prey.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.76.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.76.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The stout-hearted are spoiled, they have slept their sleep: and none of the men of might have found their hands.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.76.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.76.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "At thy rebuke, O God of Jacob, both the chariot and horse are cast into a dead sleep.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.76.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.76.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thou, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "art",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to be feared: and who may stand in thy sight when once thou art angry?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.76.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.76.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou didst cause judgment to be heard from heaven; the earth feared, and was still,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.76.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.76.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When God arose to judgment, to save all the meek of the earth. Selah.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.76.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.76.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Surely the wrath of man shall praise thee: the remainder of wrath wilt thou restrain.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.76.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.76.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Vow, and pay to the LORD your God: let all that are about him bring presents to him that ought to be feared.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.76.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.76.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He shall cut off the spirit of princes: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "he is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " terrible to the kings of the earth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
